                <div class="faq-reach-text w-richtext">
                    <div class="w-embed">
                        <section class="faq-section" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
                            <div class="faq-row">
                                <h2 class="faq-title" itemprop="headline">Got questions?</h2>
                                <ul class="faq-list-blog">

                                    <li class="faq-list-blog__item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity"
                                        itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
                                        <button class="faq-list-blog__question" aria-expanded="false">
                                            <span itemprop="name">What is a dark theme in UI?</span>
                                            <span class="faq-list-blog__icon"></span>
                                        </button>
                                        <div class="faq-list-blog__answer" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                                            itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                                            <span itemprop="text">
                                                <p>Dark mode is a display setting that uses dark backgrounds with light
                                                    text and interface elements.</p>
                                                <p>It reduces the amount of light emitted by a screen, which many users
                                                    find more comfortable. In product design, it’s treated as a separate
                                                    color theme that needs its own surface scale, typography rules, and
                                                    color treatments.</p>
                                            </span>
                                        </div>
                                    </li>

                                    <li class="faq-list-blog__item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity"
                                        itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
                                        <button class="faq-list-blog__question" aria-expanded="false">
                                            <span itemprop="name">Why do Gen Z prefer dark mode?</span>
                                            <span class="faq-list-blog__icon"></span>
                                        </button>
                                        <div class="faq-list-blog__answer" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                                            itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                                            <span itemprop="text">
                                                <p>For Gen Z, dark mode is partly a visual preference and partly a
                                                    cultural signal.</p>
                                                <p>It reduces eye strain during long screen sessions and causes less
                                                    disruption to sleep patterns at night. Aesthetically, it aligns with
                                                    the premium feel that younger audiences associate with well-designed
                                                    products. On OLED devices, it also saves battery, which is an
                                                    appreciated bonus for a young generation.</p>
                                            </span>
                                        </div>
                                    </li>

                                    <li class="faq-list-blog__item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity"
                                        itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
                                        <button class="faq-list-blog__question" aria-expanded="false">
                                            <span itemprop="name">Should you always offer a dark mode toggle?</span>
                                            <span class="faq-list-blog__icon"></span>
                                        </button>
                                        <div class="faq-list-blog__answer" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                                            itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                                            <span itemprop="text">
                                                <p>Not necessarily.</p>
                                                <p>A toggle makes sense when your product serves a broad audience with
                                                    varying preferences or when it’s used across different lighting
                                                    environments. For products with a very specific audience and context
                                                    of use, a well-considered default theme often matters more than
                                                    offering both options.</p>
                                            </span>
                                        </div>
                                    </li>

                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </section>
                    </div>
